Message_PrinterSystemLog: no <syslog.h> on wasm32-wasip1.

This file is four parallel platform chains, and the change treats them differently on purpose.

The two chains where WASI wants the answer an existing arm already gives EXTEND that arm rather
than adding one: the constructor and the destructor become
`#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__wasi__)`, because there is no openlog()/closelog() pair
to open or close, which is already true of Emscripten and Android.

The other two chains, the include block and send(), get a new `#elif defined(__wasi__)` arm INSIDE
the chain that is already there, never a parallel `#ifdef` beside it. The Emscripten arm cannot be
shared in either: it includes <emscripten/emscripten.h> and calls four EM_JS-defined console
functions that do not exist on WASI.

WHAT THE WASI BRANCH DOES: send() writes the message and a newline to stderr with fprintf() and
returns. Message_Printer::send() returns void, so no caller reads a value, and nothing in this
class reports failure to write. stderr is chosen over dropping the message because it is the one
sink a wasip1 host is guaranteed to be able to observe, and because a printer whose entire purpose
is to reach the system log must not silently discard. The message gravity is deliberately not
encoded into the line: syslog() takes a priority argument that stderr has no equivalent of, and
inventing a textual prefix would change the text the caller asked to have printed. The constructor
and destructor hold no resource, so an OSD-level "close" has nothing to do.

This class has no in-tree consumer outside Draw and DRAWEXE, which this build does not compile; it
is reachable only through an application that registers the printer itself.

Issue: https://github.com/SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift/issues/2173

diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_PrinterSystemLog.cxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_PrinterSystemLog.cxx
index 8f732da0..9bf8f3d6 100644
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_PrinterSystemLog.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_PrinterSystemLog.cxx
@@ -85,6 +85,8 @@ EM_JS(void, occJSConsoleError, (const char* theStr), {
   const aStr = Number(theStr); // bigintToI53Checked(theStr);
   console.error(UTF8ToString(aStr));
 });
+#elif defined(__wasi__)
+  #include <cstdio>
 #else
   #include <syslog.h>
 
@@ -125,7 +127,7 @@ Message_PrinterSystemLog::Message_PrinterSystemLog(
   myEventSource = (void*)RegisterEventSourceW(NULL, aWideSrcName.ToWideString());
 #elif defined(__ANDROID__)
   //
-#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__wasi__)
   //
 #else
   openlog(myEventSourceName.ToCString(), LOG_PID | LOG_NDELAY, LOG_USER);
@@ -145,7 +147,7 @@ Message_PrinterSystemLog::~Message_PrinterSystemLog()
   }
 #elif defined(__ANDROID__)
   //
-#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__wasi__)
   //
 #else
   closelog();
@@ -199,6 +201,10 @@ void Message_PrinterSystemLog::send(const TCollection_AsciiString& theString,
       return;
   }
   occJSConsoleWarn(theString.ToCString());
+#elif defined(__wasi__)
+  // wasip1 exposes no system log; stderr is the only sink the host is guaranteed to see
+  (void)theGravity;
+  fprintf(stderr, "%s\n", theString.ToCString());
 #else
   syslog(getSysLogPriority(theGravity), "%s", theString.ToCString());
 #endif
